1
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:12,920
Brighten it up and step back to look.

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,600
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling.

3
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,280
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:42,440
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:47,700
So, the tiles on the arcade street

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,500
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,880 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,080
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the aunties with blue eyeshadow too.

10
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning at that corner.

11
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,900
You can meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kame-ari
surely there is Kame-ari.

13
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,940
Everyone, come to our town!

14
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:34,600
Thank you.

15
00:01:37,020 --> 00:01:39,160
Chase after it, Kame-yari!

16
00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:48,120
I deeply apologize for
causing such a stir in society.

17
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:50,520
Well, I haven't been making a fuss,
you know.

18
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:55,000
I intend to take responsibility
for this scandal and resign.

19
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:58,640
Fine, I'll let you resign, then.

20
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:05,320
But it's no small matter!

21
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:08,900
Taking responsibility for a subordinate's scandal,
the superior has resigned.

22
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:12,540
If anything happens, I'm in a position
where I have to take responsibility too.

23
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:15,680
Especially at our station,
there's one person I'm worried about.

24
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,340
Drift car

25
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:21,140
Too dangerous for an idiot.

26
00:02:21,140 --> 00:02:22,500
An accident! It's an accident!

27
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:25,200
I'm starting to worry.

28
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:27,740
That could happen, too.

29
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:30,580
We really have to brace ourselves for this!

30
00:02:32,900 --> 00:02:34,060
Therefore,

31
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:37,820
some young people have no one
to turn to with their troubles,

32
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:41,720
and there are cases where they
end up taking irreversible actions.

33
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:43,620
To prevent that before it happens,

34
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:48,260
you must always pay close attention
to your subordinates' behavior.

35
00:02:48,260 --> 00:02:51,040
Do you have any worries,
or something like that?

36
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:53,740
Casually asking them is also important.

37
00:02:53,740 --> 00:02:55,020
Listen up, Ohara-kun.

38
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:01,520
Lately my hair keeps getting thinner,
and I've also developed a corn on my foot.

39
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:03,760
I'm not asking about your worries.

40
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:07,780
I'm asking whether you're listening to your
subordinates' worries with genuine care.

41
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:09,580
Well, that's just...

42
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:12,400
It's too late once they've caused a problem.

43
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:16,700
People who go on to cause trouble are
often big spenders in their daily lives,

44
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:18,160
borrowing money,

45
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,560
or getting hooked on gambling.

46
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:21,280
Gambling.

47
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:23,520
Do you understand, Ohara-kun?

48
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,100
If you have any idea who
such a subordinate might be,

49
00:03:31,100 --> 00:03:35,700
make sure everyone is strictly on guard,
no matter what.

50
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:38,120
Understood, Ohara?

51
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:39,000
Yes.

52
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,220
Chief Daijiro Ohara.

53
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:44,100
Even if you change your preference
to someone five foot six,

54
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:48,540
your retirement plans will be
seriously thrown off course.

55
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,080
Good morning, Chief.

56
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,360
Good morning.

57
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,520
Is Ryotsu not here?

58
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,700
Ryo-san is out on patrol.

59
00:04:01,700 --> 00:04:02,700
I see.

60
00:04:03,840 --> 00:04:07,260
By the way, has anything unusual
happened with Ryotsu recently?

61
00:04:07,260 --> 00:04:09,540
Something unusual... let me think.

62
00:04:09,540 --> 00:04:13,740
Anything at all.
I don't care how trivial it is. Tell me.

63
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:15,500
Well...

64
00:04:16,980 --> 00:04:18,280
That's right. If it's senpai...

65
00:04:18,280 --> 00:04:19,960
What is it? What happened?

66
00:04:19,960 --> 00:04:21,980
He asked me to lend him money.

67
00:04:24,540 --> 00:04:26,120
He was short on money.

68
00:04:29,140 --> 00:04:30,440
He lost at the races again,

69
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,940
and he was super upset about it.

70
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:33,120
Gambling

71
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:34,700
If it's Ryo-san,

72
00:04:35,300 --> 00:04:38,360
he's been dodging the model shop because of unpaid debts,
hasn't he?

73
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:40,040
Even sterilizing...

74
00:04:40,500 --> 00:04:41,660
No, this is bad.

75
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:44,520
He's going to cause the irreversible
problem the chief was talking about.

76
00:04:44,520 --> 00:04:47,220
The officer pattern has already begun.

77
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,320
But that's just Ryo-chan as usual.

78
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:51,520
Exactly.

79
00:04:51,520 --> 00:04:53,700
Even so, we can't relax.

80
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:55,040
What's wrong, Chief?

81
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:57,460
It's intense.

82
00:04:57,460 --> 00:05:00,140
Shut up! How could you
possibly understand how I feel?

83
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:02,740
Haven't you noticed anything else?

84
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:03,760
Anything else?

85
00:05:04,980 --> 00:05:05,420
What is it?

86
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:08,060
Come to think of it, yesterday,

87
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:09,080
Ryo-chan

88
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:12,140
Damn, my head hurts.

89
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:17,640
Senpai's head hurts.

90
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:19,480
I've never heard that before.

91
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:21,800
Ryo-tsu getting a headache, of all things!

92
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:24,020
That doesn't happen once in ten years!

93
00:05:24,020 --> 00:05:25,140
Yesterday, was it?

94
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,100
With a cornered look on his face,

95
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:30,780
"Alright, I'll do it!"

96
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:31,800
that's what he said.

97
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:33,460
There's no other choice. I have to do it.

98
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:35,460
I heard it too.

99
00:05:45,540 --> 00:05:47,340
Good morning, Chief.

100
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:52,680
Ryo-chan, what about your bicycle?

101
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:55,340
It broke, so

102
00:05:55,340 --> 00:05:56,520
I sent it in for repairs.

103
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,220
Ow

104
00:06:03,940 --> 00:06:04,860
Ryotsu

105
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,300
It's true, Chief.

106
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,020
I haven't taken anything to the
pawnshop or anything like that.

107
00:06:09,020 --> 00:06:10,800
He's acting fidgety.

108
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:12,160
He's hiding something, isn't he?

109
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:14,120
No, well, if that's the case,
then that's fine.

110
00:06:14,120 --> 00:06:15,320
Anyway, Ryotsu.

111
00:06:15,320 --> 00:06:16,260
Ryotsu.

112
00:06:16,260 --> 00:06:19,400
You don't have something
you want to tell me, do you?

113
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:22,380
No, there's nothing at all.

114
00:06:24,140 --> 00:06:25,820
So there is something after all.

115
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:31,860
I've got to get going on patrol.
Well, I'm off on patrol, then.

116
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:45,980
Hey, Nakagawa, we're tailing Ryotsu.

117
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:47,280
Y-yes, sir.

118
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,540
Are we tailing him in this car?

119
00:06:53,540 --> 00:06:57,460
If we used a Ferrari, he'd sense it was me.

120
00:06:57,900 --> 00:06:59,660
I went with a more low-key Countach.

121
00:07:00,580 --> 00:07:01,300
Low-key?

122
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:03,660
There he is.

123
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:05,480
Follow him.

124
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,040
Yes.

125
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:10,700
The Countach is so cool.

126
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:14,440
What are you doing, passing him?

127
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:17,020
I thought I was driving
at a low speed, though.

128
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:26,160
Driving like that, you'll wreck the engine.

129
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:30,100
He went into somewhere.

130
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:34,240
He went into the pawnshop.

131
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:36,040
Is he planning to borrow money?

132
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:42,420
He's coming out.

133
00:07:46,740 --> 00:07:49,380
Looks like he couldn't borrow it there.

134
00:07:49,380 --> 00:07:53,240
But now it's clear he's
really hard up for cash.

135
00:07:58,060 --> 00:07:58,900
Damn it!

136
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:24,260
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

137
00:08:24,260 --> 00:08:31,080
Mid-engine, space-frame structure... wow, it really
is amazing. Liquid-cooled V12, DOHC, 48 valves.

138
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:36,880
Hey, bro, nice car you've got there.
Thanks. Drive safely.

139
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:39,720
Yeah, nice.

140
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:47,560
What's with those two, two guys in a car together half-naked?
Better not get involved with them.

141
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:53,000
Nakagawa, you look like an idiot.

142
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,360
So does the Chief.

143
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:00,640
I still haven't paid it back.

144
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:05,180
That looked like Ryo-san just now.

145
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,780
He ducked into the old man's place.

146
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:09,640
Follow him!

147
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:12,340
Chasing him through such a
narrow place in a Countach!

148
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:15,420
He's noticed we're tailing
him and is trying to lose us.

149
00:09:17,020 --> 00:09:18,000
Understood.

150
00:09:28,380 --> 00:09:30,160
See, you can do it after all.

151
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:33,160
Hey, I'm getting fired up now!

152
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:35,360
It's like we're sanding the car down,
you know.

153
00:09:40,820 --> 00:09:42,780
So he came through here.

154
00:09:42,780 --> 00:09:44,460
He's like a stray cat, isn't he.

155
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:47,220
Well, looks like the chase ends here.

156
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:54,900
Thanks to the low ground clearance,

157
00:09:54,900 --> 00:09:56,540
even jumping over things is fine

158
00:09:56,940 --> 00:09:59,740
If the Lamborghini's engineers saw this,
they'd cry.

159
00:10:04,580 --> 00:10:05,200
Are they still there?

160
00:10:05,200 --> 00:10:08,620
Found him!

161
00:10:09,220 --> 00:10:10,900
If we go out in front, he'll spot us.

162
00:10:10,900 --> 00:10:11,780
Don't worry.

163
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:13,800
We're blending in perfectly
with the camouflage.

164
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:16,840
Good point.

165
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:21,200
He's talking to the takoyaki guy.

166
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:26,720
No way.

167
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,100
What's wrong?

168
00:10:30,100 --> 00:10:31,720
He's squeezing money out of him.

169
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,320
What a guy.

170
00:10:33,320 --> 00:10:36,360
No way... Senpai really would go that far?

171
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,360
It may already be too late.

172
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,700
We should have said something sooner.

173
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,580
I really regret that.

174
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:06,300
I can already see his downfall.

175
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:08,560
He's moving again.

176
00:11:08,560 --> 00:11:08,940
Hey.

177
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,300
What is that car?

178
00:11:13,300 --> 00:11:14,580
Is that even a car?

179
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:16,040
Aren't you going to scrap it?

180
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:17,260
It's filthy.

181
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:20,440
We have to contact the ward office about this,
you know.

182
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:29,900
Chief, what about this building?

183
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:33,140
It's a land speculator
with all kinds of problems.

184
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:36,080
I never imagined Senpai would be
going in and out of a place like this.

185
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,460
What?!

186
00:11:49,860 --> 00:11:53,060
No, no, look,
that restaurant over there, the Ohara...

187
00:11:54,320 --> 00:11:56,500
What a coincidence, it's Ohara too.

188
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:05,800
Chief?

189
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:09,960
It's all my fault for not doing enough.

190
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:14,140
I should have seen Ryotsu
going down the wrong path.

191
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:15,760
They've come out.

192
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,020
I'll persuade him to turn himself in.

193
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:32,180
Terri-ri-chi-nu

194
00:12:32,180 --> 00:12:37,360
What are you doing in a place like this?

195
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:43,340
You don't perhaps have
something to say to Hashi, do you?

196
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:47,220
Uh-oh, when I visited the
Chief's house the other day...

197
00:12:47,220 --> 00:12:50,160
Did they find out I broke the painted plate?

198
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:52,720
No, there's nothing at all.

199
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:56,900
You're definitely hiding something.

200
00:12:56,900 --> 00:12:59,380
But we can't let this happen here.

201
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:02,520
Well, it's not right to chat
standing around here like this.

202
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:04,740
Let's go somewhere quiet.

203
00:13:04,740 --> 00:13:10,480
Hey, Ryotsu.

204
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:15,800
Everyone has secrets they can't tell others.

205
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:16,980
Just as I thought.

206
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:21,440
Especially if you regret that you did wrong.

207
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:22,120
Plate.

208
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:29,280
But no matter how cleverly you think you've covered it up,
secrets always come out eventually.

209
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:33,880
I see...
darn, you've figured it out, haven't you.

210
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:36,900
At first, it's just a little curiosity.

211
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:38,300
That's right.

212
00:13:38,300 --> 00:13:41,480
I also started out of just a
little curiosity and got involved.

213
00:13:41,480 --> 00:13:43,840
Before long, it gradually escalated.

214
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:46,340
By the time you realize you've messed up,
it's too late.

215
00:13:47,760 --> 00:13:49,600
I thought I'd messed up too.

216
00:13:50,220 --> 00:13:52,900
Why didn't you tell me right away?

217
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:55,420
Well, I figured you'd scold me, Chief.

218
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,740
Don't be silly.

219
00:13:56,740 --> 00:13:58,340
Even if I did scold you,

220
00:13:58,340 --> 00:14:00,320
it's only because I'm thinking of you.

221
00:14:00,320 --> 00:14:02,780
I'm scolding you with a heart of a demon.

222
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:04,520
So you'll forgive me, then?

223
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:06,480
Forgive or not, it doesn't come into it.

224
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:09,780
What a subordinate does is also the
responsibility of his superior, me.

225
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:14,240
Thank goodness. If the Chief says so,
I can finally rest easy.

226
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:20,080
It seems you held back just in time
from stepping onto the path of evil.

227
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:22,500
Right, let's push him hard.

228
00:14:25,380 --> 00:14:26,360
Ryotsu.

229
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:30,900
I'm always thinking about you.

230
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:31,420
Chief.

231
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:36,060
So let's talk a bit more about our futures,
shall we?

232
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:38,400
Our futures, Chief...?

233
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:39,620
RYOTSU!

234
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:45,180
Wh-wait a second, Chief!

235
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:50,080
What a beautiful sky, Ryotsu.

236
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:53,097
Ryotsu,

237
00:14:53,147 --> 00:14:57,120
I have a past too.

238
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:58,940
What are you trying to say?

239
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:02,220
So it's not enough, but I'll do what I can.

240
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:05,900
I'm partly responsible
for you being single, too.

241
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:16,580
Come to think of it, we're a community of fate.
We're not exactly a married couple who's been together for ages, but from now on, no more secrets, got it?

242
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:25,580
Wait, we're not that kind of relationship. Yeah, I can tell from your eyes.
Even without you saying anything, your feelings come through painfully clear.

243
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:25,940
Hey.

244
00:15:25,940 --> 00:15:31,800
Ahhh, no way! I can't believe
the Chief has a hobby like that!

245
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:38,560
You can't just dump your car
in a place like this, buddy.

246
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:41,200
I'm not dumping it, I'm just stopping here.

247
00:15:42,020 --> 00:15:44,760
Honestly, first Maria, now the Chief...

248
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:47,220
Why do only men keep coming on to me?

249
00:15:47,740 --> 00:15:49,480
Why don't women ever fall for me?

250
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,780
When I'm such a handsome guy?

251
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:56,060
You're not that popular!

252
00:15:56,500 --> 00:15:58,760
Don't do anything rash!

253
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:04,900
Ryotsu! Just listen to me!

254
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:07,620
No thank you, Chief,
I'm fine with your talk!

255
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:09,880
Where on earth are you going?!

256
00:16:10,620 --> 00:16:12,220
To the bank, I said the bank!

257
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:14,860
The bank...

258
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,600
What business do you have at the bank!

259
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:20,640
Money, of course! What else would it be!

260
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:22,300
That's not allowed!

261
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:26,000
That's exactly why you have to stop!
You said you'd consult me about anything!

262
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,880
I'm an adult too, you know!

263
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:31,340
So, between adults, between men,
about our friendship, but...

264
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:34,200
I can't keep up with you anymore, Chief!

265
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:35,560
Ryotsu!

266
00:16:35,940 --> 00:16:39,320
Ryotsu...

267
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:41,280
Ryotsu!

268
00:16:42,980 --> 00:16:45,940
Hurry! Ryotsu's going to rob the bank!

269
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:49,460
If we don't hurry,
the bank's going to close!

270
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:55,000
No...

271
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:57,880
Chief!

272
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:07,300
Please, just let me go, Chief.

273
00:17:07,840 --> 00:17:09,360
Think again, Ryotsu.

274
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:11,380
It's not all your fault.

275
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:13,820
It's because I couldn't go with everyone.

276
00:17:13,820 --> 00:17:16,160
This has nothing to do with you, Chief.

277
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:18,460
Is there really no way
you'll listen to what I say?

278
00:17:18,460 --> 00:17:21,160
Of course not. If I say no, then it's no.

279
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:24,320
Fine, then I'm prepared too.

280
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:29,120
If you're so set on it,
you'll have to get past me first.

281
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:31,580
Chief.

282
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:34,420
R-Ryo... Ryotsu.

283
00:17:35,420 --> 00:17:36,400
Chief!

284
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:39,420
Chief!

285
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:42,480
Come and jump into my arms!

286
00:17:43,120 --> 00:17:43,800
Right?

287
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:46,100
Whoa! Too bad!

288
00:17:46,100 --> 00:17:47,520
Ryotsu!

289
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:56,700
Chief! Chief!

290
00:17:57,640 --> 00:18:00,340
Nakagawa,
contact the station and call for backup.

291
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:03,660
If he's really going to rob a bank,
there's no stopping him now.

292
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:05,640
Eek, a cockroach!

293
00:18:05,640 --> 00:18:07,880
Don't make such a fuss over a cockroach.

294
00:18:13,920 --> 00:18:15,860
Hey, one, two, three...

295
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:19,040
Something's going on outside. It's so noisy.

296
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:32,120
I warned you so many times,
and you've finally gone and done it.

297
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:43,440
I'm sorry, we almost talked him out of it, but what a mess.
Chief, let me try to persuade him. Can you do that?

298
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,180
Yes!

299
00:18:46,160 --> 00:18:47,760
Ryotsu, can you hear me?

300
00:18:48,580 --> 00:18:49,940
222322

301
00:18:49,940 --> 00:18:52,780
It's the Chief again.
You're being way too persistent.

302
00:18:54,180 --> 00:18:58,760
Ryotsu,
do you remember the first time you met me?

303
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:02,400
You had only just
graduated from high school.

304
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:08,280
When you became a police officer and
your mother asked me to look after you,

305
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:10,980
I remember it as clearly
as if it were yesterday.

306
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:12,440
What is this?

307
00:19:14,180 --> 00:19:18,200
Just in time! With the power of my love,
I'll reform you into a fine man!

308
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:22,580
Your mother must be
weeping to see you like this!

309
00:19:24,240 --> 00:19:30,680
Mother knitted me gloves
late into the night.

310
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:32,200
Why are you singing Mother's song?

311
00:19:32,200 --> 00:19:35,840
Aaaah... the cold winter wind is blowing.

312
00:19:36,160 --> 00:19:42,300
...she knitted them diligently, you know.

313
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:52,400
News from my hometown came from far away,
smelling of the hearth fire.

314
00:19:53,780 --> 00:19:57,900
Ryotsu, come back to me.

315
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:00,540
I don't know what's going on, but...

316
00:20:02,200 --> 00:20:02,860
I can't obtain it.

317
00:20:04,680 --> 00:20:06,080
That's enough, Ohara.

318
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:07,540
There's no other choice.

319
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:09,120
Charge in!

320
00:20:18,320 --> 00:20:19,200
W-what is this?

321
00:20:23,380 --> 00:20:24,140
We've arrested him.

322
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,940
300,000 yen a month.

323
00:20:25,940 --> 00:20:27,120
was about to rob it.

324
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:28,880
No, that's mine,

325
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:30,080
Shut up! Along with the whole bank!

326
00:20:30,080 --> 00:20:31,260
The whole bank!

327
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:34,780
Ryo-chan!

328
00:20:38,020 --> 00:20:39,740
Senior, it's a shame.

329
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:42,320
Ryo-san,
I'll bring you some rice balls, okay?

330
00:20:42,320 --> 00:20:43,560
Hey, wait a minute!

331
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:44,980
What did I do wrong?

332
00:20:44,980 --> 00:20:46,400
Hey! Let go of me! Hey!

333
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,160
Ryo-san!

334
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:50,460
Thanks, Ryo-san.

335
00:20:50,460 --> 00:20:52,900
You talked things over with
the real estate agent for us,

336
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:56,520
so that children's plaza is
going to stay just as it is, right?

337
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:58,560
Now we can play soccer there again!

338
00:20:58,560 --> 00:21:00,600
By the way, Ryo-san, what happened to you?

339
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,860
Don't ask.

340
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:05,200
Before I knew what was happening,
they made me out to be a bank robber.

341
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:07,260
What children's plaza?

342
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:09,300
The one that was about to be
forced out by land speculators?

343
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:12,340
So then,
the extortionist real estate agency...

344
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:14,980
What are you talking about, Ohara-kun?

345
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:19,440
This man didn't commit any bank robbery.

346
00:21:19,440 --> 00:21:21,420
That's what I've been saying!

347
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:24,640
When we checked the records
of the cash handling system,

348
00:21:25,080 --> 00:21:26,740
the 300,000 yen he was carrying

349
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:29,640
turned out to be his own
salary he had withdrawn.

350
00:21:29,640 --> 00:21:30,520
See? Told you so.

351
00:21:33,260 --> 00:21:34,360
Ohara-kun

352
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:38,860
It happened yesterday.

353
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:41,540
As usual, while I was on patrol,

354
00:21:41,540 --> 00:21:44,640
I was napping inside the pipe at the plaza

355
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:47,140
What?

356
00:21:47,740 --> 00:21:48,540
That hurts!

357
00:21:49,020 --> 00:21:51,680
So that's why your head was hurting.

358
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,360
What did you think it was from?

359
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:55,320
Hmph.

360
00:21:56,280 --> 00:22:00,540
Well, if you listen, the kids are saying they'll have nowhere to play,
and that's a real problem.

361
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:03,580
I made up my mind to
strip down and get serious.

362
00:22:04,340 --> 00:22:06,080
On the way,
at the takoyaki shop, the other day

363
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:08,240
I collected the part-time pay
for watching the shop for them

364
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:10,440
I got my part-time pay.

365
00:22:10,440 --> 00:22:11,560
Right?

366
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,200
What did you think it was?

367
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:16,140
After that, I took a shortcut

368
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:17,600
through the Sarakin building

369
00:22:17,600 --> 00:22:20,260
and went to the landlord's house behind it.

370
00:22:20,260 --> 00:22:21,260
A shortcut.

371
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:22,740
Is that so?

372
00:22:22,740 --> 00:22:25,940
And I asked the landlord to keep
that place open for the children

373
00:22:25,940 --> 00:22:28,780
just as it has been,
and I got him to promise it.

374
00:22:29,320 --> 00:22:30,180
Well, if you just talk to him,

375
00:22:30,180 --> 00:22:31,980
he's a pretty reasonable old guy,

376
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:33,920
and he agreed right away.

377
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:36,340
So then I took another shortcut

378
00:22:36,340 --> 00:22:37,640
Meow.

379
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:38,300
Meow, meow.

380
00:22:38,300 --> 00:22:41,960
and went to settle things with the Jiyagiya.

381
00:22:42,780 --> 00:22:44,500
Th-those shady dealings

382
00:22:45,120 --> 00:22:46,560
Well...

383
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:49,100
So everything was settled,

384
00:22:49,100 --> 00:22:52,160
and I went to the bank in high spirits.

385
00:22:52,740 --> 00:22:54,300
That makes sense.

386
00:22:54,300 --> 00:22:55,760
I see.

387
00:22:56,260 --> 00:22:57,420
Ohara-kun.

388
00:22:57,420 --> 00:22:58,940
I'm terribly sorry.

389
00:22:58,940 --> 00:22:59,520
Brother.

390
00:22:59,520 --> 00:23:02,180
So this was all the Chief
jumping to conclusions

391
00:23:02,180 --> 00:23:03,900
Nakagawa, you too!

392
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,640
Joe! This is Switch Gen!

393
00:23:05,700 --> 00:23:06,980
Chief, three servings!

394
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:10,520
Thanks, thanks. Get the bill from this guy.

395
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:12,720
My darling!

396
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:14,300
That'll be 15,000 yen!

397
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:16,680
Hey, collect the fees!

398
00:23:17,420 --> 00:23:21,360
Being mistaken for a criminal
has left my heart in shreds!

399
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:22,975
and they even slapped handcuffs on me,

400
00:23:23,025 --> 00:23:26,100
how am I supposed to heal
these wounds from here on?

401
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,960
Fine, fine, I'll pay, all right?

402
00:23:29,580 --> 00:23:32,740
But there was something
that didn't sit right...

403
00:23:34,420 --> 00:23:35,580
By the way, Ryotsu...

404
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,820
when I first called out to you,

405
00:23:37,820 --> 00:23:39,480
why were you so flustered?

406
00:23:43,540 --> 00:23:45,360
Kameari Park police box, hello?

407
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:48,080
It's for you, Chief. It's from your wife.

408
00:23:48,080 --> 00:23:50,260
It's me.

409
00:23:50,980 --> 00:23:53,220
What? The plate from Mari's set is broken?

410
00:23:53,780 --> 00:23:55,480
There are traces of glue where
it was stuck back together.

411
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:58,760
Come to think of it,
Ryotsu came over to our house the other day.

412
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:04,120
Ryo-san! So it was you after all!

413
00:24:04,580 --> 00:24:05,720
I'm sorry!

414
00:24:05,960 --> 00:24:09,140
This is all because your
everyday behavior is terrible!

415
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:11,540
Get serious and shape up!

416
00:24:12,320 --> 00:24:15,220
Yes, sir! I'm reflecting on my actions!

417
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:35,460
Every train ride,
love at first sight from Dad's back

418
00:24:36,780 --> 00:24:41,980
Hard work again this week,
unreasonable is only reasonable

419
00:24:43,140 --> 00:24:46,680
Bucket in hand, playing it cool

420
00:24:46,680 --> 00:24:49,400
Beef bowl, extra broth, cloudy as can be

421
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:52,760
Overtime after overtime, the irritation too

422
00:24:52,760 --> 00:24:56,400
Ylang-ylang clears it all up, gone

423
00:24:59,880 --> 00:25:06,120
Every day, eyes on Robben,
a girl like me, I love me

424
00:25:06,120 --> 00:25:12,920
Every day, eyes on Robben,
hearts flying on Monday

425
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:16,380
Monday, Monday, Robobull

426
00:25:20,180 --> 00:25:22,220
Good evening, this is Shoji Murakami

427
00:25:22,220 --> 00:25:24,780
Stop it already, right hand,
left hand, both hands

428
00:25:24,780 --> 00:25:26,640
Welcome, arm come, somewhere chest

429
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:29,640
Pervert! Stop! Dad, please, let him go!

430
00:25:29,780 --> 00:25:31,440
What are you saying? Hayami says!

431
00:25:31,880 --> 00:25:33,640
What's that, that! Armpit, that too!

432
00:25:34,380 --> 00:25:37,740
Next time: Ryo-san runs in the election!
Nice to meet you!

